The Home Screen interface is vertically structured from top to bottom, comprising the status bar, widgets, an application icon grid, a page search utility, and the dock.
•	Status Bar (Top Tier): Spanning the uppermost portion of the display from left to right:
o	Time: Displays the local time as 09:25. Positioned to its right is the silent mode icon.
o	Dynamic Island: The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator.
o	Connectivity & Power: The cellular signal strength icon displays three solid white bars and one gray bar, followed by the network type indicator ("5GUW") (OR The Airplane Mode icon denotes that wireless network transmissions are currently disabled.). The adjacent battery icon appears partially filled alongside the digital percentage readout "62."
Below the status bar, a pair of application widgets are displayed: on the left, the Weather widget displays the text "Weather Unavailable"; on the right, the Calendar widget displays the text "TUESDAY 6 No events today." Below the widgets, applications are arranged across a flexible grid system, where each application icon consists of a graphic identifier paired with a text label displaying the application name.
Positioned just above the Dock is a persistent Search button. Pinned to the bottom of the Home Screen is the Dock—a fixed, translucent horizontal container housing four application icons.
